<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor solved on a cellular PIN-permeability lattice, with a growing dividing cellular lattice and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 bending (Friml 2002, Band 2012) (Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella statocytes))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-6> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella statocytes)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Vertex or Cellular Potts wall mechanics, cell-wall viscoplasticity, 3D curvature, quantitative reproduction of digitised Grieneisen (2007) or Mähönen (2014) figure data, or quantitative model-to-micrograph matching beyond order-of-magnitude meristem cell number",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Empirical CV segmentation of the 3-panel Arabidopsis root meristem confocal micrograph (`arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 1527x513 px): N = 113 DAPI nuclei, spacing 18.34 +- 0.58 px SE, apical/proximal nuclear density ratio 1.118 (unchanged from Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gravistimulation as a g-biased PIN3/PIN7 statocyte efflux split k_col(1 +- g) on the central columella files with Sachs sine law g = g_max sin(phi), auxin-inhibited epidermal elongation and a curvature integral with Band (2012) tipping-point reset at 40 degrees (`simulate_gravitropic_bending`): lateral auxin ratio 1.85 (ref 2.0 +- 0.7), tipping point reached at 5.55 h (ref 2 +- 1 h, disclosed slow), pin3 bending-rate fraction 0.52 (ref 0.5 +- 0.25)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Growing 9-file cellular lattice with explicit mitotic division of PLETHORA-high cells at 2 x birth length and auxin-independent elongation of PLETHORA-intermediate cells (`simulate_growing_cellular_lattice`): 23 divisions in 10 h, 26 meristem cells (ref 32 +- 6), 82 um/h growth (ref 180 +- 80, disclosed low), 0.958 cells/h/file (ref 1.5 +- 0.7)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mähönen (2014) PLETHORA finite-volume solver on variable-length rows with meristem dilution ln2/17 h folded into turnover (`solve_plethora_gradient`, `zone_boundaries`): WT z_MZ = 240 um, z_EZ = 390 um; decap 225, pin2 120, k_lat = 0 45, NPA 480 (saturated, disclosed disagreement), ablation 255 um",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Solved steady-state cellular PIN-permeability transport operator on a 32-row x 9-file lattice (`build_pin_lattice_operator`, `solve_cellular_auxin_steady_state`) with Law 1 counter-current flux and closed-operator mass conservation verified on the real operator (column-sum error < 1e-12); all six regimes EMERGENT: WT 113.6x shoot concentration at z = 52.5 um, shoot decapitation retaining 92.5 %, pin2 (v_e = 0) 0.46x WT, lateral-PIN ablation k_lat = 0 collapsing to 0.18x WT, NPA 1.10x shoot, QC laser ablation + Xu (2006) respecification regenerating the maximum at 112.5 um (+60 um)",
        "reported_in_source: Beemster & Baskin (1998) Plant Physiol 116:1515 cell division and elongation kinetics of the Arabidopsis root (cell cycle ~17-18 h, mature cortical cell ~160 um); Dello Ioio et al. (2007) Curr Biol 17:678 meristem cortical cell number ~30",
        "reported_in_source: Friml et al. (2002) Nature 415:806-809 and Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) PNAS 107:22344 gravity-induced lateral relocation of PIN3/PIN7 in columella statocytes producing a lower/upper lateral auxin asymmetry; Band et al. (2012) PNAS 109:4668 transient lateral auxin gradient dissipating at a ~40 degree tipping point",
        "reported_in_source: Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449:1008-1013 cellular root apex reverse-fountain auxin reflux loop (rootward PIN1 stele permeability v_s, apolar columella PIN3/PIN4/PIN7 redistribution k_col, shootward PIN2 epidermal/LRC permeability v_e, inward lateral reflux k_lat on epidermis/cortex/endodermis) generating a >100-fold Quiescent Center auxin maximum that persists after shoot decapitation and regenerates proximally after QC laser ablation (Xu et al. 2006)",
        "reported_in_source: Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515:125-129 slow auxin-induced PLETHORA synthesis, cell-to-cell movement, and growth dilution creating an axial PLT dosage gradient whose thresholds Theta_MZ = 0.36 and Theta_EZ = 0.14 position the meristematic, elongation and differentiation zones",
        "transfer_boundary: Rectangular cellular compartments with uniform row lengths across the 9 files; growth and bending are reduced kinematic models (no wall mechanics, no vertex/CPM), and the Pass-1 reference-table six-regime values are synthetic calibration targets, not digitised paper data" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Arabidopsis thaliana" ;
