<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor solved on a cellular PIN-permeability lattice, with a growing dividing cellular lattice and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 bending (Friml 2002, Band 2012) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Grieneisen (2007) cellular PIN-permeability reflux model is now actually solved (`build_pin_lattice_operator` L178-288 assembles the sparse operator with rootward stele, shootward epidermal, inward lateral and apolar columella permeabilities, passive exchange, turnover and the shoot source; `solve_cellular_auxin_steady_state` L291-295), the Mähönen (2014) PLETHORA solver runs on variable-length rows with growth dilution (`solve_plethora_gradient` L334-362), the growing lattice divides cells explicitly (`simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` L542-636) and gravistimulation is a g-biased statocyte efflux split (L253-263) feeding sine-law bending (`simulate_gravitropic_bending` L641-716). Six machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) cover the laws. Two points below v2 because the v2 remediation asked for vertex/CPM mechanics and the delivered growth/bending are reduced kinematic models with uniform row lengths and an imposed 40 degree tipping point." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
