<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Vascular-Epidermal Counter-Current Reflux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves the pairwise cancellation of internal transfer terms and hence exact mass conservation of the closed reflux lattice; the script checks it numerically as zero column sums (max |Σ| / max |entry| = 0) of the assembled sparse operator plus a steady-state flux budget on the open operator | Variables: A_i: cellular auxin concentration; V_i = l_i w: cell area; c_ij: passive (D·face/dist) plus PIN-permeability (p_ij·face) transport coefficient from cell i to j; σ, μ: biosynthesis and turnover; J_in: shoot vascular influx" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Methods & Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L178-L325>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L31-L53> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def stele_reflux_rhs (dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_s + k_lat * A_e - mu * A_s
def epidermis_reflux_rhs (dJ_e k_lat A_e mu : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_e - k_lat * A_e - mu * A_e
theorem grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation
    (dJ_s dJ_e k_lat A_s A_e mu J_tip : Int) :
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs dJ_e k_lat A_e mu =
      -(dJ_s + dJ_e) - mu * (A_s + A_e) ∧
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e 0 A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs (-dJ_s) k_lat A_e 0 = 0 ∧
    cross_section_net_flux J_tip (-J_tip) = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d(V_i A_i)/dt = Σ_j [c_ji A_j − c_ij A_i] + σ V_i − μ V_i A_i;  with μ = σ = J_in = escape = 0 every column of the operator sums to zero (Σ_i d(V_i A_i)/dt = 0, J_stele + J_epidermis = 0 across the closed tip)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.stele_reflux_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Quiescent Center (QC) Reflux Capacitor Amplification vs NPA / Lateral-PIN Ablation Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Qualitative Lean model of the capacitor; the script now produces the amplification, its position and its collapse by solving the operator (Pass 2 hard-coded them) | Variables: A_QC: emergent stele auxin maximum at the QC/columella boundary; A_shoot: top-row stele concentration; v_s, v_e, k_lat, k_col: PIN permeabilities (µm/s)" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L375-L537>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L72-L95> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def qc_two_stage_capacitor (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int) : Int :=
  A_shoot * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat) * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat)
theorem grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse
    (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int)
    (hA : A_shoot > 0) (hvs : v_s > 0) (hve : v_e > 0) (hklat : k_lat > 0) :
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat > A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e 0 = A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot 0 0 k_lat = A_shoot
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_QC / A_shoot ≫ 1 emerges from v_s, v_e, k_lat, k_col > 0 (solved: 113.6× at z = 52.5 µm);  k_lat = 0 → A_QC drops to 0.18 × WT;  NPA (all p → 3-5 %) → A_QC / A_shoot = 1.10" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.qc_two_stage_capacitor" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mähönen et al. (2014) PLETHORA (PLT1/2) Dosage Gradient & Meristem Boundary Monotonicity Law" ;
    dct:description "Positions the meristematic and elongation zone boundaries from the solved auxin field; emergent WT z_MZ = 240 µm, decapitated 225, pin2 120, k_lat=0 45, QC-ablation 255 (NPA: PLT saturates everywhere — disclosed disagreement) | Variables: P_k: PLT dosage of row k; α: synthesis rate (1/h); γ: turnover (1/h); r_k: relative growth (dilution) rate; D_plt: cell-to-cell movement (µm²/h); Θ_MZ, Θ_EZ: zone thresholds" ;
    dct:source "Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515(7525):125-129 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L330-L372>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L110-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plethora_axial_dosage (alpha_plt G_reflux beta_decay z : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - beta_decay * z
def meristem_boundary_coord (alpha_plt G_reflux Theta_MZ : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - Theta_MZ
theorem mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity
    (alpha_plt G1 G2 beta_decay z Theta_MZ : Int)
    (h_alpha : alpha_plt > 0) (h_gain : G2 > G1) :
    plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G2 beta_decay z >
      plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G1 beta_decay z ∧
    meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G2 Theta_MZ >
      meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G1 Theta_MZ
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "l_k dP_k/dt = α H(A_k) l_k − (γ + r_k) l_k P_k + F_{k+1/2} − F_{k−1/2},  H(A) = A²/(K² + A²),  F = D_plt (P_{k+1} − P_k)/d;  z_MZ = top of last row with P ≥ Θ_MZ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.plethora_axial_dosage" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Friml et al. (2002) / Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Columella Efflux Asymmetry Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the gravistimulated split conserves columella efflux, strictly favours the lower side for g > 0 and is monotone in g; the solved lattice then yields an EZ lower/upper epidermal auxin ratio of 1.85 at g_max = 0.18 (Spearman ρ = 1.0 over the g sweep) that drives sine-law bending (tipping point reached at 5.55 h vs Band's ≈2 h — disclosed) | Variables: k_col: apolar columella PIN3/4/7 permeability; g ∈ [0, 1]: statocyte relocalisation asymmetry; φ: tip inclination from the gravity vector; β: bending angle; β_tip: Band (2012) tipping point" ;
    dct:source "Friml et al. (2002) Nature 415(6873):806-809; Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) PNAS 107(51):22344-22349; Band et al. (2012) PNAS 109(12):4668-4673" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L641-L716>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L147-L176> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lower_side_permeability (k_col g : Int) : Int := k_col * (1 + g)
def upper_side_permeability (k_col g : Int) : Int := k_col * (1 - g)
def lateral_efflux_asymmetry (k_col g : Int) : Int :=
  lower_side_permeability k_col g - upper_side_permeability k_col g
theorem friml_2002_gravistimulated_columella_efflux_asymmetry
    (k_col g g1 g2 : Int) (hk : k_col > 0) (hg : g > 0) (hmono : g2 > g1) :
    lower_side_permeability k_col g + upper_side_permeability k_col g = 2 * k_col ∧
    lower_side_permeability k_col g > upper_side_permeability k_col g ∧
    lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g = 2 * k_col * g ∧
    lower_side_permeability k_col 0 = upper_side_permeability k_col 0 ∧
    lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g2 > lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p_lower = k_col (1 + g),  p_upper = k_col (1 − g),  p_lower + p_upper = 2 k_col,  p_lower − p_upper = 2 k_col g (monotone in g),  g = g_max sin(φ)·[β < β_tip]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.lateral_efflux_asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.friml_2002_gravistimulated_columella_efflux_asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mähönen et al. (2014) PLETHORA Growth-Dilution Monotonicity Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the growth-dilution mechanism used by `solve_plethora_gradient` on the growing lattice: elongating rows dilute PLT faster and exit the meristem, which is what positions the EZ/DZ boundary in `simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` | Variables: P: PLT dosage; S = α H(A): auxin-induced synthesis; γ: turnover; r: relative growth rate of the cell row (ln2/T_cycle in the meristem, r_ez (1 − l/l_mature) in the elongation zone)" ;
    dct:source "Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515(7525):125-129 Figs. 3-4 (growth dilution of PLT proteins)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L334-L362>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L188-L203> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plt_dilution_balance (P gamma r : Int) : Int := P * (gamma + r)
theorem mahonen_2014_plethora_growth_dilution_monotone
    (P1 P2 gamma r1 r2 S : Int)
    (_hP1 : P1 > 0) (hP2 : P2 > 0) (hgamma : gamma > 0) (hr1 : r1 ≥ 0) (hr : r2 > r1)
    (h1 : plt_dilution_balance P1 gamma r1 = S) (h2 : plt_dilution_balance P2 gamma r2 = S) :
    P2 < P1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P (γ + r) = S  ⇒  r₂ > r₁ ≥ 0 ∧ γ > 0 ∧ P₁, P₂ > 0  ⇒  P₂ < P₁" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.plt_dilution_balance" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mahonen_2014_plethora_growth_dilution_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Explicit Mitotic Division Length-Conservation Law of the Growing Cellular Lattice (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees the division rule of `simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` conserves file length and never creates sub-birth-length daughters; the script's self-test checks the same invariants on the 24 h run (23 divisions, 26 meristem cells, min length ≥ l_birth) | Variables: l: meristematic cell row length; l_birth: daughter length at birth (7 µm); n_cells: number of rows in the file" ;
    dct:source "Beemster & Baskin (1998) Plant Physiol 116(4):1515-1526 (kinematic cell production); Dello Ioio et al. (2007) Curr Biol 17(8):678-682 (meristem cell number)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L542-L636>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L213-L229> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def daughter_a (l : Int) : Int := l / 2
def daughter_b (l : Int) : Int := l - l / 2
theorem mitotic_division_length_conservation
    (l l_birth n_cells : Int) (_hb : l_birth > 0) (hl : l ≥ 2 * l_birth) :
    daughter_a l + daughter_b l = l ∧
    daughter_a l ≥ l_birth ∧
    daughter_b l ≥ l_birth ∧
    (n_cells - 1) + 2 = n_cells + 1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "l ≥ 2 l_birth ∧ l_birth > 0  ⇒  ⌊l/2⌋ + (l − ⌊l/2⌋) = l ∧ ⌊l/2⌋ ≥ l_birth ∧ l − ⌊l/2⌋ ≥ l_birth ∧ n_cells → n_cells + 1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.daughter_a" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mitotic_division_length_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Vascular-Epidermal Counter-Current Reflux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves the pairwise cancellation of internal transfer terms and hence exact mass conservation of the closed reflux lattice; the script checks it numerically as zero column sums (max |Σ| / max |entry| = 0) of the assembled sparse operator plus a steady-state flux budget on the open operator | Variables: A_i: cellular auxin concentration; V_i = l_i w: cell area; c_ij: passive (D·face/dist) plus PIN-permeability (p_ij·face) transport coefficient from cell i to j; σ, μ: biosynthesis and turnover; J_in: shoot vascular influx" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Methods & Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L178-L325>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L31-L53> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def stele_reflux_rhs (dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_s + k_lat * A_e - mu * A_s
def epidermis_reflux_rhs (dJ_e k_lat A_e mu : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_e - k_lat * A_e - mu * A_e
theorem grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation
    (dJ_s dJ_e k_lat A_s A_e mu J_tip : Int) :
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs dJ_e k_lat A_e mu =
      -(dJ_s + dJ_e) - mu * (A_s + A_e) ∧
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e 0 A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs (-dJ_s) k_lat A_e 0 = 0 ∧
    cross_section_net_flux J_tip (-J_tip) = 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d(V_i A_i)/dt = Σ_j [c_ji A_j − c_ij A_i] + σ V_i − μ V_i A_i;  with μ = σ = J_in = escape = 0 every column of the operator sums to zero (Σ_i d(V_i A_i)/dt = 0, J_stele + J_epidermis = 0 across the closed tip)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.stele_reflux_rhs" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Quiescent Center (QC) Reflux Capacitor Amplification vs NPA / Lateral-PIN Ablation Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Qualitative Lean model of the capacitor; the script now produces the amplification, its position and its collapse by solving the operator (Pass 2 hard-coded them) | Variables: A_QC: emergent stele auxin maximum at the QC/columella boundary; A_shoot: top-row stele concentration; v_s, v_e, k_lat, k_col: PIN permeabilities (µm/s)" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L375-L537>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L72-L95> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def qc_two_stage_capacitor (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int) : Int :=
  A_shoot * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat) * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat)
theorem grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse
    (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int)
    (hA : A_shoot > 0) (hvs : v_s > 0) (hve : v_e > 0) (hklat : k_lat > 0) :
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat > A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e 0 = A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot 0 0 k_lat = A_shoot
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_QC / A_shoot ≫ 1 emerges from v_s, v_e, k_lat, k_col > 0 (solved: 113.6× at z = 52.5 µm);  k_lat = 0 → A_QC drops to 0.18 × WT;  NPA (all p → 3-5 %) → A_QC / A_shoot = 1.10" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.qc_two_stage_capacitor" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mähönen et al. (2014) PLETHORA (PLT1/2) Dosage Gradient & Meristem Boundary Monotonicity Law" ;
    dct:description "Positions the meristematic and elongation zone boundaries from the solved auxin field; emergent WT z_MZ = 240 µm, decapitated 225, pin2 120, k_lat=0 45, QC-ablation 255 (NPA: PLT saturates everywhere — disclosed disagreement) | Variables: P_k: PLT dosage of row k; α: synthesis rate (1/h); γ: turnover (1/h); r_k: relative growth (dilution) rate; D_plt: cell-to-cell movement (µm²/h); Θ_MZ, Θ_EZ: zone thresholds" ;
    dct:source "Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515(7525):125-129 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L330-L372>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L110-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plethora_axial_dosage (alpha_plt G_reflux beta_decay z : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - beta_decay * z
def meristem_boundary_coord (alpha_plt G_reflux Theta_MZ : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - Theta_MZ
theorem mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity
    (alpha_plt G1 G2 beta_decay z Theta_MZ : Int)
    (h_alpha : alpha_plt > 0) (h_gain : G2 > G1) :
    plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G2 beta_decay z >
      plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G1 beta_decay z ∧
    meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G2 Theta_MZ >
      meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G1 Theta_MZ
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "l_k dP_k/dt = α H(A_k) l_k − (γ + r_k) l_k P_k + F_{k+1/2} − F_{k−1/2},  H(A) = A²/(K² + A²),  F = D_plt (P_{k+1} − P_k)/d;  z_MZ = top of last row with P ≥ Θ_MZ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.plethora_axial_dosage" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Friml et al. (2002) / Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Columella Efflux Asymmetry Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the gravistimulated split conserves columella efflux, strictly favours the lower side for g > 0 and is monotone in g; the solved lattice then yields an EZ lower/upper epidermal auxin ratio of 1.85 at g_max = 0.18 (Spearman ρ = 1.0 over the g sweep) that drives sine-law bending (tipping point reached at 5.55 h vs Band's ≈2 h — disclosed) | Variables: k_col: apolar columella PIN3/4/7 permeability; g ∈ [0, 1]: statocyte relocalisation asymmetry; φ: tip inclination from the gravity vector; β: bending angle; β_tip: Band (2012) tipping point" ;
    dct:source "Friml et al. (2002) Nature 415(6873):806-809; Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) PNAS 107(51):22344-22349; Band et al. (2012) PNAS 109(12):4668-4673" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L641-L716>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L147-L176> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lower_side_permeability (k_col g : Int) : Int := k_col * (1 + g)
def upper_side_permeability (k_col g : Int) : Int := k_col * (1 - g)
def lateral_efflux_asymmetry (k_col g : Int) : Int :=
  lower_side_permeability k_col g - upper_side_permeability k_col g
theorem friml_2002_gravistimulated_columella_efflux_asymmetry
    (k_col g g1 g2 : Int) (hk : k_col > 0) (hg : g > 0) (hmono : g2 > g1) :
    lower_side_permeability k_col g + upper_side_permeability k_col g = 2 * k_col ∧
    lower_side_permeability k_col g > upper_side_permeability k_col g ∧
    lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g = 2 * k_col * g ∧
    lower_side_permeability k_col 0 = upper_side_permeability k_col 0 ∧
    lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g2 > lateral_efflux_asymmetry k_col g1
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p_lower = k_col (1 + g),  p_upper = k_col (1 − g),  p_lower + p_upper = 2 k_col,  p_lower − p_upper = 2 k_col g (monotone in g),  g = g_max sin(φ)·[β < β_tip]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.lateral_efflux_asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.friml_2002_gravistimulated_columella_efflux_asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mähönen et al. (2014) PLETHORA Growth-Dilution Monotonicity Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the growth-dilution mechanism used by `solve_plethora_gradient` on the growing lattice: elongating rows dilute PLT faster and exit the meristem, which is what positions the EZ/DZ boundary in `simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` | Variables: P: PLT dosage; S = α H(A): auxin-induced synthesis; γ: turnover; r: relative growth rate of the cell row (ln2/T_cycle in the meristem, r_ez (1 − l/l_mature) in the elongation zone)" ;
    dct:source "Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515(7525):125-129 Figs. 3-4 (growth dilution of PLT proteins)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L334-L362>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L188-L203> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plt_dilution_balance (P gamma r : Int) : Int := P * (gamma + r)
theorem mahonen_2014_plethora_growth_dilution_monotone
    (P1 P2 gamma r1 r2 S : Int)
    (_hP1 : P1 > 0) (hP2 : P2 > 0) (hgamma : gamma > 0) (hr1 : r1 ≥ 0) (hr : r2 > r1)
    (h1 : plt_dilution_balance P1 gamma r1 = S) (h2 : plt_dilution_balance P2 gamma r2 = S) :
    P2 < P1
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P (γ + r) = S  ⇒  r₂ > r₁ ≥ 0 ∧ γ > 0 ∧ P₁, P₂ > 0  ⇒  P₂ < P₁" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.plt_dilution_balance" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mahonen_2014_plethora_growth_dilution_monotone" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Explicit Mitotic Division Length-Conservation Law of the Growing Cellular Lattice (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees the division rule of `simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` conserves file length and never creates sub-birth-length daughters; the script's self-test checks the same invariants on the 24 h run (23 divisions, 26 meristem cells, min length ≥ l_birth) | Variables: l: meristematic cell row length; l_birth: daughter length at birth (7 µm); n_cells: number of rows in the file" ;
    dct:source "Beemster & Baskin (1998) Plant Physiol 116(4):1515-1526 (kinematic cell production); Dello Ioio et al. (2007) Curr Biol 17(8):678-682 (meristem cell number)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L542-L636>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L213-L229> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def daughter_a (l : Int) : Int := l / 2
def daughter_b (l : Int) : Int := l - l / 2
theorem mitotic_division_length_conservation
    (l l_birth n_cells : Int) (_hb : l_birth > 0) (hl : l ≥ 2 * l_birth) :
    daughter_a l + daughter_b l = l ∧
    daughter_a l ≥ l_birth ∧
    daughter_b l ≥ l_birth ∧
    (n_cells - 1) + 2 = n_cells + 1
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "l ≥ 2 l_birth ∧ l_birth > 0  ⇒  ⌊l/2⌋ + (l − ⌊l/2⌋) = l ∧ ⌊l/2⌋ ≥ l_birth ∧ l − ⌊l/2⌋ ≥ l_birth ∧ n_cells → n_cells + 1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.02.047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/415806a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1013145107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1201498109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.116.4.1515>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1121790> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Solved 2D Cellular PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Permeability Transport Lattice (Vascular–Epidermal Reverse-Fountain Reflux Capacitor) with Finite-Volume PLETHORA Zonation, Explicit Mitotic Division on a Growing Lattice, and Gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 Statocyte Efflux Asymmetry" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.daughter_a" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mitotic_division_length_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1>,
